<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Pharsalus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/48-bce">48 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Pharsalus was fought on 9 August 48 BCE near Pharsalus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and the larger army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> and the Senate. Caesar's veterans routed Pompey's cavalry and then his infantry, and Pompey fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he was murdered. The victory decided the main phase of the civil war and made Caesar master of the Roman world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-pharsalus.jpg" alt="Battle of Pharsalus" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Department of History, United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Pharsalus,_48_BC.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
